Long time lurker, first post.

I just had a rather good Archaeologist taken from me. I was doing a lot
better than I normally do, thanks to some RNG luck, but she giveth and
she taketh away.

I knew this was going to be an interesting game when I found Frost
Brand on DL1. Frost Brand! I'd never seen it before! Shame Arc are
restricted in long sword... but adopting the old "try it and see"
technique, it seemed rather good.

At turn 1929, still quite shallow in the DoD, I found an "AoR. A wand
of polymorph left me with a pet green dragon shortly afterwards, and
then I found a tool shop with 2 bags of holding. I was a little
disappointed that I would no longer get a big reward from sokoban, but
I had some pretty good kit.

The green dragon killed all the minetown guards, shopkeepers and the
priest. I had already bought 2 points of protection, so I got my money
back. Unfortunately I lost them again when I sacrificed a gnome,
forgetting my own race... and it took quite a while to find big enough
corpses to mollify my god. Still, I thought to myself, it's a mistake
but not a game-killer. Shame I couldn't think of any other way to get
myself some protection.

I wasted some polymorph charges polypiling non-magical armour before I
remembered the distinction; then some elven boots and cloaks provided
me with a nice [oMR to go with my "oR.

Back to the DoD, and down to sokoban. Sokoban was an excercise in
self-control, since although I knew I could defeat everything there, I
had to duck back into corridors and run away downstairs to heal up an
awful lot.

Back to mines end, by which time I was getting fairly unstoppable. I
didn't bother mapping out the dark levels, just heading straight for
the downstairs. Somewhere around this time I got teleportitis from a
tengu.

Shortly afterwards, my pet dragon kindly moved my minetown stash from
its nicely Elberethed square to somewhere where a gelatinous cube could
engulf it. That was annoying.

Found a b?oG, killed off L. Not that I've ever met an L, but y'know. A
spellbook of create monster helped me get Magicbane, which I
dual-wielded with a silver saber. Another polypiling session (hoping
for magic markers) gave me a saddle, which I placed on Wurble the
dragon.

I got the Titan medusa level, but it was rather easy because Magicbane
cancelled the titan before it summoned any nasties. However, I hadn't
had the foresight to pick up any grease so I wasn't going anywhere near
a ; any time soon. Alas, Wurble was overexcited and went to a watery
grave. Thinking better, I dug down with my pickaxe, going straight
through the mazes to the castle, figuring I'd get that WoW. However,
when I played ABCDE on my tooled horn, nothing happened. When I played
FFFGG also, nothing happened.

At this point, my game had progressed very little in the last 20k
moves. I had -4 AC, 106 max HP, XL 14. I was trapped between castle and
medusa (I'm not sure if I had the means to levelport, I had TC at this
point). I headed back up through the mazes, and found a brown H. I
thought "Ho hum, I can deal with a giant."

The minotaur hits you! You die...

Overall, I think I did well. I aquired teleportitis and telecontrol
intrinsics, had +2 leather gloves, +1 high boots, +0 [oMR, +0 dwarvish
mithril-coat, and a +0 helm of brilliance. Why such poor armour?
Because in the whole game, I came across precisely 0 ?oEA. That would
have been my first wish from the castle wand.

But, as with a lot of games, I felt I was stuck in a rut, constantly
managing and remanaging inventory, not quite able to proceed without
extreme caution and Elberething, only -4 AC and 106 HP and no obvious
way to decrease AC.

How do you proceed once you get to this point? Can't go further, can't
stay where you are...



